section('ia','06 Sitemap and page structure',p('The route inventory is the proposed full concept website. It is not a claim that these pages already exist. The candidate Philadelphia page remains visibly research-only until an exact city/type and source inventory are approved. No other jurisdiction page should masquerade as coverage.')+table(['Route','Page','Required narrative','Hero and visual direction'],routes))

section('navigation','07 Navigation and buyer journeys',p('<strong>Desktop:</strong> CivicSubmittal logo · Products · Platform · Solutions · Coverage · Pricing · Resources · Company · Sign in · Discuss a pilot. Use grouped menus to fit the header: Products contains all five named modules and “All products”; Resources contains Sources, Pilot evaluation and Guides; Company contains About, Contact and Responsibility. Coverage stays prominent. At narrower desktop widths collapse secondary groups before crowding the CTA.')+p('<strong>Footer:</strong> five products; Platform/Features; three audiences; Coverage/Sources; Pricing/Pilot/Request demo; Company/Contact/Trust; Resources/Research notes; Privacy/Terms; Sign in/Access help. Include LinkedIn and Crunchbase marks with accessible inactive “Profile not yet provided” text until real URLs exist. No meaningless # links, invented addresses or third-party builder branding.')+p('<strong>Mobile:</strong> same destinations in labeled expandable groups; 44px minimum practical targets, keyboard focus containment, Escape/dismiss, restored focus, and body-scroll restoration.')+table(['Visitor','Journey','Successful outcome'],[
('Builder operations buyer','Home scope gate → Review page → Pilot evaluation → Pricing → Pilot request','A qualified upcoming-packet conversation with explicit city/type and proposed fee.'),
('Expediting principal','Expediter solution → Desk/Review/Proof → synthetic TI-107 → Pilot','Understands differentiated applicant-side work and agrees to discuss a scoped test.'),
('Architect','Architect solution → TI-107 evidence pane → Trust/Sources','Can inspect assumptions and retain decision control; can flag a source correction.'),
('Unsupported visitor','Scope gate → unsupported explanation → official resources or coverage-interest form','Understands no current support; may consent to updates without being counted as a qualified pilot.'),
('City official','Trust → Sources → official-portal handoff','Can see no claim of affiliation, delegated authority or replacement of the city portal.')]))

